## Why this happens

When Excel cells are prefixed with `'` (apostrophe), Excel treats the value as text — but when pandas reads it with `openpyxl`, that apostrophe is sometimes preserved in the string value. So `'nissan nv'` becomes the literal string `'nissan nv` in the DataFrame, which doesn't match the search term `nissan nv`.

The `applymap` warnings are a separate issue — that's a **pandas version deprecation** (pandas ≥ 2.1 replaced `applymap` with `map`). For those, find every `.applymap(` in `Submit_2_Helper_function.py` inside `find_transfer_price_adjustment`, `tax_and_public`, `operating_profit`, `energy_tgk_68`, and replace with `.map(`.
